From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] plat: intel: agilex5: make the FPGA-config address contract
 round-trip

On Agilex 5, BL31 cannot be driven through FPGA_CONFIG_WRITE by a caller
that uses the buffer BL31 itself advertises:

1. INTEL_SIP_SMC_FPGA_CONFIG_GET_MEM returns 0x80400000..0x82000000
   (INTEL_SIP_SMC_FPGA_CONFIG_ADDR / _SIZE), but intel_fpga_config_write()
   rejects every address below BL31_LIMIT (0x82000000) through
   is_address_in_ddr_range(). Every buffer inside the advertised window
   returns INTEL_SIP_SMC_STATUS_REJECTED. On Agilex 7 the window is
   0x400000..0x2000000 and BL31_LIMIT is 0x81000, so the two agree there.

2. intel_smmu_hps_remapper_init() subtracts DRAM_BASE from the buffer
   address before it is stored, and FPGA_CONFIG_COMPLETED_WRITE returns
   the stored value. A caller that submitted physical address P gets
   P - 0x80000000 back and cannot match it to the buffer it sent.

Linux's stratix10-svc legacy path (every kernel up to v7.3, and the
"intel,agilex-svc" / "intel,stratix10-svc" match entries after that)
does exactly this: it builds its pool from GET_MEM, submits physical
addresses and looks completions up by the same value. With (1) the first
data submit is rejected; with only (1) fixed, (2) leaves every buffer
locked and the FPGA manager spins.

Accept a buffer that lies wholly inside the GET_MEM window, and return
the caller's own address from COMPLETED_WRITE.

The second half is conditional. Altera's downstream kernels and Linux
v7.4's "intel,agilex5-svc" path submit IOVA + 0x80000000 and expect the
bare IOVA back, and both announce themselves by requesting remapper
bypass (INTEL_SIP_SMC_FCS_SDM_REMAPPER_CONFIG, x1 = 1) at probe. Record
that request -- independently of the JTAG-ID gate that decides whether
the remap registers are written -- and keep today's return value for
those callers. Like g_remapper_bypass, the record is never cleared
before the next reset. U-Boot's "fpga load" only counts non-zero
completions and is unaffected either way.

The acceptance change is not conditional. A bypass caller's buffer that
lies wholly in 0x80400000..0x81ffffff after the offset (an IOVA of
0x400000..0x1ffffff) used to be rejected and is now accepted. Those are
valid addresses in such a caller's IOVA space, which ends at 0x20000000.

is_address_in_ddr_range() itself is not widened, so no other SMC gains
access below BL31_LIMIT, and 0x80000000..0x803fffff (BL31 itself) stays
rejected.

Provenance
----------
Origin:       this repo. Found by reading v2.15.0 against Linux 7.3.4's
              drivers/firmware/stratix10-svc.c and drivers/fpga/
              stratix10-soc.c; docs/de25-vendor-kernel-delta.md section 3
              has the trace.
Author:       this repo.
Upstream:     Candidate. Not submitted; whether and when is the owner's
              call. v2.12.0 (Terasic's base) and TF-A master carry the
              same two behaviours.
Why carried:  without it mainline Linux cannot program the Agilex 5
              fabric through BL31 in any SMMU configuration, and the
              alternative is a carried kernel patch.
Verified:     [V] applies at -F0 to v2.15.0 after 0001; bl31.bin builds
              for PLAT=agilex5 and PLAT=agilex (aarch64 gcc 15.2), with
              __BL31_END__ unchanged at 0x800178c0; a host harness of the
              patched functions passes the accept/reject and round-trip
              cases listed in docs/de25-vendor-kernel-delta.md.
              [U] any behaviour on hardware -- no DE25-Nano has run this
              image.

Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 plat/intel/soc/common/socfpga_sip_svc.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/intel/soc/common/socfpga_sip_svc.c b/plat/intel/soc/common/socfpga_sip_svc.c
--- a/plat/intel/soc/common/socfpga_sip_svc.c
+++ b/plat/intel/soc/common/socfpga_sip_svc.c
@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@
 static bool bridge_disable;
 #if PLATFORM_MODEL == PLAT_SOCFPGA_AGILEX5
 static uint32_t g_remapper_bypass;
+/* Set once a caller asks for remapper bypass, whatever the silicon. */
+static bool g_remapper_bypass_requested;
 #endif
 
 /* RSU static variables */
@@ -152,6 +154,15 @@
 				current_block++;
 				*buffer_addr_completed =
 					fpga_config_buffers[i].addr;
+#if PLATFORM_MODEL == PLAT_SOCFPGA_AGILEX5
+				/*
+				 * No bypass request: the caller sent a physical
+				 * address, and the stored one lacks DRAM_BASE.
+				 */
+				if (!g_remapper_bypass_requested) {
+					*buffer_addr_completed += DRAM_BASE;
+				}
+#endif
 				return 0;
 			}
 		}
@@ -328,14 +339,32 @@
 	return true;
 }
 
+#if PLATFORM_MODEL == PLAT_SOCFPGA_AGILEX5
+/*
+ * The window INTEL_SIP_SMC_FPGA_CONFIG_GET_MEM advertises lies below
+ * BL31_LIMIT. INTEL_SIP_SMC_FPGA_CONFIG_SIZE is its end address.
+ */
+static bool is_fpga_config_get_mem_window(uint64_t addr, uint64_t size)
+{
+	return (addr >= INTEL_SIP_SMC_FPGA_CONFIG_ADDR) &&
+	       (addr < INTEL_SIP_SMC_FPGA_CONFIG_SIZE) &&
+	       (size <= (INTEL_SIP_SMC_FPGA_CONFIG_SIZE - addr));
+}
+#endif
+
 static uint32_t intel_fpga_config_write(uint64_t mem, uint64_t size)
 {
 	int i;
+	bool addr_ok;
 
 	intel_fpga_sdm_write_all();
 
-	if (!is_address_in_ddr_range(mem, size) ||
-		is_fpga_config_buffer_full()) {
+	addr_ok = is_address_in_ddr_range(mem, size);
+#if PLATFORM_MODEL == PLAT_SOCFPGA_AGILEX5
+	addr_ok = addr_ok || is_fpga_config_get_mem_window(mem, size);
+#endif
+
+	if (!addr_ok || is_fpga_config_buffer_full()) {
 		return INTEL_SIP_SMC_STATUS_REJECTED;
 	}
 
@@ -807,6 +836,10 @@
 
 int intel_smmu_hps_remapper_config(uint32_t remapper_bypass)
 {
+	if (remapper_bypass == 0x01) {
+		g_remapper_bypass_requested = true;
+	}
+
 	/* Read out the JTAG-ID from boot scratch register */
 	if (is_agilex5_A5C0() || is_agilex5_A5C4()) {
 		if (remapper_bypass == 0x01) {
